cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >
  If you use CliMed in research, please cite this software release
  and the associated scientific publications when available.

title: "CliMed: Climate-Informed Mechanistic Modelling Framework for Dengue Risk"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Prasad"
    given-names: "Peri Subrahmanya Hari"
    affiliation: "Centre for Oceans, Rivers, Atmosphere and Land Sciences (CORAL), Indian Institute of Technology Kharagpur, India"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-20"

repository-code: "https://github.com/pshari19/CliMed"
url: "https://github.com/pshari19/CliMed"

abstract: >
  CliMed is a climate-informed mechanistic modelling framework developed
  for spatial and temporal assessment of Aedes mosquito ecology and dengue
  transmission potential under observed and changing climatic conditions.
  The framework integrates climate, environmental and spatial information
  with biologically based mosquito-host transmission processes and produces
  mechanistic indicators including entomological inoculation rate (EIR),
  force of infection (FOI), infection probability, vector-to-host ratio
  and infectious-vector fraction. CliMed was developed by Dr. Peri
  Subrahmanya Hari Prasad under the academic guidance and supervision of
  Prof. A. N. V. Satyanarayana, Centre for Oceans, Rivers, Atmosphere and
  Land Sciences (CORAL), Indian Institute of Technology Kharagpur, India.

